course: dictionary
lesson: 8251
title: Rhyming words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Words rhyme when their ending sounds are the same. «cat» and «hat» rhyme, and so do «light» and «night». You listen to the end of the word, not the start, so «cat» and «dog» do not rhyme.
explain: A rhyme can also be a short poem or song with rhyming words, like a nursery rhyme. «Thirty days hath September, April, June and November» is a famous rhyme that helps people remember the days in each month. «Hath» is old English for «has».
explain: Poems do not always rhyme. Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat, but the poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause, so it is still poetry and not just chopped-up prose.
fact: Rhymes are words whose ending sounds match, like «cat» and «hat».
fact: A rhyme is also a short poem or song with rhyming words, like a nursery rhyme.
fact: Rhyme helps people remember things, which is why children learn nursery rhymes.
fact: «Une souris verte» is a silly rhyme about a green mouse running in the grass; it says «verte», not «vert», because «souris» is feminine.
fact: Rhyme has a phrase too: «without rhyme or reason» means with no sense at all.
exercise: Which word rhymes with «light»? | door | sun | dog | *night
exercise: In «Thirty days hath September», what does «hath» mean? | *Has | Hat | Hurt | Hate
exercise: Which pair of words rhymes? | cup and dog | tree and table | red and sun | *hop and top
test: What is a rhyme? | A word that starts with the same letter | A word that means the same as another word | A very long story | *A word that rhymes with another word
test: What is a nursery rhyme? | *A short poem or song with rhyming words | A map of a town | A long novel | A cooking recipe
exam: Free verse has no regular rhyme or beat. Is it still poetry? | Yes, because every line ends with the same sound | No, only rhyming lines are poetry | *Yes, the poet breaks the lines where the reader should pause | No, it is chopped-up prose
